Email DLQ



The consumer retries K times with exponential backoff:

Attempt 1 → Fail → Wait 1 sec
Attempt 2 → Fail → Wait 2 sec
Attempt 3 → Fail → Wait 4 sec
...
Attempt K → Fail

The exponential backoff is important because if the provider is already overloaded or temporarily down, we don't want thousands of consumers continuously retrying immediately, which could make the problem worse.

After K retries, if the notification still cannot be delivered:

Email Consumer
      ↓
K retries + Exponential Backoff
      ↓
Still Failed
      ↓
DLQ

So our design has:

Retry → Try again
Exponential Backoff → Wait progressively longer between retries
DLQ → Store messages that failed after all retries for later investigation/reprocessing.


