We suddenly receive 100,000 notifications per second.
One Email Consumer instance can process only 1,000 notifications/second.
How would you scale the Email Consumer to handle this increased load?


If a Kafka topic has 10 partitions, a single consumer group can have at most 10 actively consuming consumers for that topic.


10 Partitions
      ↓
10 Consumers → Each consumer gets 1 partition



If you have 20 consumers:

10 Consumers → Active
10 Consumers → Idle

So to scale consumers beyond 10, you need to increase the number of partitions.
One nuance: the number of consumers does not have to equal the number of partitions. 
You can have fewer consumers than partitions, and each consumer will handle multiple partitions.




If the current Email Topic has:

10 partitions

and you need more parallel consumers, you can increase the number of partitions:

10 partitions
      ↓
Increase
      ↓
50 partitions
      ↓
Up to 50 active consumers

So:

Email Topic
├── P0 → Consumer 1
├── P1 → Consumer 2
├── P2 → Consumer 3
├── ...
└── P49 → Consumer 50



Kafka automatically handles partition assignment/rebalancing when consumers join or leave a consumer group.


